menu "sys_event"

    config SYS_EVENT_MAX_SUBS
        int "Subscriptions (C)"
        default 32
        range 4 255
        help
          Listeners made by C code: inline ones (a device's ON_EVENT) and
          queued ones (the VM, the power manager; the event task).

    config SYS_EVENT_QUEUE_BYTES
        int "Queue (bytes)"
        default 1024
        range 256 16384
        help
          Room of the ring buffer for events waiting for the event task (for
          the queued listeners, events from ISRs and deferred publishes). An
          event takes the buffer's 8 B, its own 4 B, its 20 B header and
          its payload. A multiple of 4. A full buffer drops the event.

    config SYS_EVENT_DATA_MAX
        int "Largest payload (bytes)"
        default 64
        range 8 256
        help
          The most bytes of an event's payload (a text of a screen's object).
          A larger payload in an events table fails to compile.

    config SYS_EVENT_TASK_PRIO
        int "Task priority"
        default 6
        range 1 24
        help
          Above the router work task (5), below the urgent task (15).

    config SYS_EVENT_TASK_STACK
        int "Task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 3072 32768
        help
          Runs the queued listeners (the VM, the power manager) and every
          listener of an ISR or deferred event: device ON_EVENT ops (I2C).

endmenu
